{"nodes": [{"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_accessibility", "label": "Web Accessibility", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L10-L12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accessibility and SEO are not competing priorities; both make a site clearer and easier to navigate, so improving one naturally helps the other."}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_seo", "label": "SEO", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L10-L12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Search optimization usually improves the experience for real people; search engines reward clarity, structure, and usability that accessibility also requires."}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_semantic_html", "label": "Semantic HTML", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L16-L32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use elements that describe content (header, nav, main, footer) instead of generic divs so screen readers and search engines can understand page structure; one h1 per page with ordered headings."}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_alt_text", "label": "Image Alt Text", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L34-L42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_meta_tags", "label": "Meta Description Tags", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L44-L53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_aria", "label": "ARIA Roles and Labels", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L55-L120", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use ARIA only when standard HTML falls short; overusing roles creates more problems than it solves. Prefer WAI-ARIA practices for complex UI like modals and tabs."}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_core_web_vitals", "label": "Core Web Vitals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L57-L65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_lcp", "label": "LCP (Largest Contentful Paint)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_cls", "label": "CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_inp", "label": "INP (Interaction to Next Paint)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_contrast_wcag", "label": "Text Contrast / WCAG", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L69-L71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_accessibility_seo_guide_mobile_first", "label": "Mobile-First Design", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/accessibility-seo-guide.md", "source_location": "L95-L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale":